/*
 * Declares the SliceConcatValue class.
 *
 * SliceConcatValue represents the concatenation of two slice values. The
 * operator produces a new slice containing the elements of the left operand
 * followed by the elements of the right operand.
 *
 * This differs from SliceAppendValue, which models an append operation where
 * the resulting slice is intended to be written back into the left operand,
 * enabling additional optimizations when the left operand is mutable.
 *
 * <hr>
 *
 * @Package: ymirc
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::generator::value::operator::slice::concat
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/generator/value/operator/slice/concat.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created(YYYY-MM-DD): 2021-11-20
 * @Copyright(C) 2021–2026 GNU-Ymir
 * @License
 *   ```text
